{"title":"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ff392ca96c48d056b01841914cd28e50128c04d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 3x + 4x = 12 + 9 + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9acada73d69e502f2cca63cb2c4450e4ce0822b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 6 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 10 \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"414\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Combining the terms on the left and right sides, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/8/558780e71f47b73cec38e12e96de72ac30704b43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/3/823f670b7d233c6fce92f30a3850a863ed6785c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{27}{9} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can order the coefficients from greatest to least, like the terms on the right side of the equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/037401793a611942d8f35bc917879eacca47f655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x + 3x + 2x = 12 + 9 + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"210\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can notice that the numbers on the right are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the coefficients on the left. This can only occur if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c082673121d8da7274f7d8a27031a6cdb9c82e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"92\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat\">2006 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a>